  "node_type": "statement",
  "body": {
    "id": "lem:moving-offset-carter-geometry",
    "kind": "lemma",
    "statement": "Fix a rational compact polytope \\(C\\subset\\mathbb R^d\\).  Suppose the multinomial interior, base-convergence, and compact local-expansion conditions hold, \\(c_n,\\widehat c_n\\) lie eventually in one compact subset of \\(\\mathcal K_0\\), and \\(\\|\\widehat c_n-c_n\\|_\\infty\\leq\\xi_n\\).  Define\n\\[\n d_n(C)=\\sup_{u\\in C}\\left\\|\\sqrt n\\{p_n(u)-p_n(0)\\}-Bu\\right\\|_2,\n \\qquad\n \\delta_n(C)=\\max_{j\\in\\mathcal J_0^{\\mathrm{act}}}\\sup_{u\\in C}|e_{n,j}(u)|,\n\\]\nwith the maximum equal to zero for an empty active list, and put \\(\\chi_n(C)=d_n(C)+\\delta_n(C)+\\xi_n\\).  Let a supplied rational number \\(\\overline\\chi_n(C)\\) satisfy \\(\\overline\\chi_n(C)\\geq\\chi_n(C)\\).  For any supplied Gaussian rule \\(G_n\\) on the completed offset regions \\(D_v^0(\\widehat c_n)\\), suppose its Gaussian semantic coverage is at least \\(1-\\eta_0-\\alpha_n\\) and its normalized separated risk is at most \\(R_n^G+\\beta_n\\).  Then a parameter-independent Carter transfer produces a multinomial rule \\(K_n\\) on \\(C\\) with semantic coverage at least\n\\[\n 1-\\eta_0-\\alpha_n-\\Delta_n(C)\n\\]\nand normalized separated risk at most\n\\[\n R_n^G+\\beta_n+\\Delta_n(C),\n\\]\nwhere\n\\[\n \\Delta_n(C)=C_{2/\\kappa}\\frac{|\\mathcal J|\\log|\\mathcal J|}{\\sqrt n}\n +\\operatorname{Err}_{\\Sigma,n}(C)\n +(H_C+2A_0)\\overline\\chi_n(C),\n \\qquad\n A_0=\\sum_{j\\in\\mathcal J_0^{\\mathrm{act}}}\n \\frac{2}{\\sqrt{2\\pi}\\{a_j'\\Sigma_0a_j\\}^{1/2}}.\n\\]\nHere coverage and risk are restricted respectively to \\(D_{n,v}\\cap C\\) and \\(H_{n,r_0}\\cap C\\).  The conclusion is unconditional on effective compatible density and does not assert that the supplied Gaussian rule has a finite certificate.",
