      "lem:bounded-semantic-transfer-by-tv"
    ],
    "proof_tex": "\\textbf{Technique: exact affine-slack coupling and a linear Gaussian anti-concentration charge.}\nFor every active facet,\n\\[\n \\zeta_{n,j}(u)-(\\widehat c_{n,j}+a_j'u)\n =(c_{n,j}-\\widehat c_{n,j})+e_{n,j}(u).\n \\tag{60}\n\\]\nConsequently the uniform slack perturbation on \\(C\\) is at most \\(\\delta_n(C)+\\xi_n\\leq\\overline\\chi_n(C)\\).  The finite completed-arrangement lemma, on the common compact offset set, matches each actual coverage role and each separated-risk role to its \\(\\widehat c_n\\)-offset counterpart with Mahalanobis displacement at most \\(H_C\\overline\\chi_n(C)\\), after the finite directed-Hausdorff and separated-set restoration constants are included in \\(H_C\\).  Equality faces lose no label because they belong to every incident completion.\n\nFor \\(W_0\\sim N_d(h,\\Sigma_0)\\), the scalar \\(\\widehat c_{n,j}+a_j'W_0\\) has variance \\(a_j'\\Sigma_0a_j>0\\).  Its density is bounded uniformly in its mean by \\(\\{2\\pi a_j'\\Sigma_0a_j\\}^{-1/2}\\).  Therefore, for \\(s\\geq0\\),\n\\[\n \\Pr_h\\{|\\widehat c_{n,j}+a_j'W_0|\\leq s\\}\n \\leq\\min\\left\\{1,\n \\frac{2s}{\\sqrt{2\\pi}\\{a_j'\\Sigma_0a_j\\}^{1/2}}\\right\\}.\n \\tag{61}\n\\]\nThe union bound and \\(\\min\\{1,z\\}\\leq z\\) give\n\\[\n \\mathfrak b_0(s)\\leq A_0s.\n \\tag{62}\n\\]\nUse the supplied enclosure as the comparison threshold, \\(\\tau_n=\\overline\\chi_n(C)\\).  Since \\(\\chi_n(C)\\leq\\tau_n\\), the indicator \\(\\mathbf1\\{\\chi_n(C)>\\tau_n\\}\\) is zero.  Every sign mismatch is contained in a band of width at most \\(\\tau_n+\\chi_n(C)\\leq2\\overline\\chi_n(C)\\), so (62) charges it by\n\\[\n \\mathfrak b_0\\{\\tau_n+\\chi_n(C)\\}\n \\leq2A_0\\overline\\chi_n(C).\n \\tag{63}\n\\]\n\nOn \\(C\\), the positive-cell proposition supplies Carter's parameter-independent kernel with error \\(C_{2/\\kappa}|\\mathcal J|\\log|\\mathcal J|/\\sqrt n\\).  To expose the covariance replacement, put \\(D_n=\\operatorname{diag}\\{p_n(0)\\}\\), \\(\\Sigma_n=\\{B'D_n^{-1}B\\}^{-1}\\), and apply to the matched normal vector \\(Y_n\\) the score map\n\\[\n S_n(Y_n)=\\Sigma_nB'D_n^{-1}\n \\frac{Y_n-np_n(0)}{\\sqrt n}.\n\\]\nIts mean is \\(\\Sigma_nB'D_n^{-1}\\sqrt n\\{p_n(u)-p_n(0)\\}\\), and its covariance is\n\\[\n \\Sigma_nB'D_n^{-1}\n [\\operatorname{diag}\\{p_n(u)\\}-p_n(u)p_n(u)']\n D_n^{-1}B\\Sigma_n.\n\\]\nThe compact local expansion and the compact covariance lemma bound the total variation from \\(N_d(u,\\Sigma_0)\\) by the explicitly defined Hellinger term \\(\\operatorname{Err}_{\\Sigma,n}(C)\\).  Gaussian translation for the matched means and the arrangement displacement contributes \\(H_C\\overline\\chi_n(C)\\).  Apply the bounded semantic-transfer lemma to the indicator \\(\\mathbf1\\{v\\in A\\}\\) and to \\(\\ell_0(A)\\in[0,1]\\).  Adding the Carter, covariance, displacement, and band charges in their outward directions gives\n\\[\n \\Delta_n(C)=C_{2/\\kappa}\\frac{|\\mathcal J|\\log|\\mathcal J|}{\\sqrt n}\n +\\operatorname{Err}_{\\Sigma,n}(C)\n +(H_C+2A_0)\\overline\\chi_n(C).\n \\tag{64}\n\\]\nAdding (64) to the supplied Gaussian coverage deficit \\(\\alpha_n\\) and risk excess \\(\\beta_n\\) proves the two asserted inequalities.  This proof begins with an arbitrary supplied Gaussian rule and nowhere invokes compatible density or CertGlue.",
    "justification": "This separates the unconditional experiment comparison from the unresolved construction of a finite certified Gaussian rule.",
    "gap": "It accepts a supplied Gaussian rule and does not prove effective compatible density.",
    "consumer": "The moving-offset theorem adds conditional CertGlue replayability to this unconditional linear comparison bound.",
